<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Zambia privatisation agency to sell three sawmills.</title>
<headline>Zambia privatisation agency to sell three sawmills.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Zambia Privatisation Agency (ZPA) said on Thursday it was inviting competitive tender bids for state-run Zambia Forestry and Forest Industries Corp's three sawmills and wood products operations.</p>
<p>The three mills, at Kafubu, Kalibu and Dola Hill, will be sold on an individual basis, the ZPA said in an advertisement placed in the South African press.</p>
<p>The ZPA gave no financial details of the operations but said combined sales of timber from the three mills averaged around 71,000 cubic metres a year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
